{"task": "Prove exactly this local conditional obligation using the supplied NL route. Return only the tactic body through submit_transition. All displayed parameter and input proof binders are already in context.", "packet": {"version": 2, "contract_sha256": "3575d5d75c1eb2aaf8b92e3182b02e09afba2fd0f4d1ab9e569e2cc16c872495", "header": "import Mathlib

open scoped ENNReal NNReal BigOperators

abbrev YuiEucl (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)
def YuiI : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 1
def YuiSnoc {n : ℕ} (x : YuiEucl n) (t : ℝ) : YuiEucl (n + 1) :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (Fin.snoc (fun i => x i) t)
def YuiHead {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : YuiEucl n :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i : Fin n => z i.castSucc)
def YuiLast {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : ℝ := z (Fin.last n)
def YuiCylinder {n : ℕ} (E : Set (YuiEucl n)) : Set (YuiEucl (n + 1)) :=
  {z | YuiHead z ∈ E ∧ YuiLast z ∈ YuiI}
noncomputable def YuiCost {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] {ι : Type*}
    (s : ℝ) (U : ι → Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∑' i, ⨆ (_ : (U i).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s
def YuiCover {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] (δ : ℝ) (A : Set X)
    (U : ℕ → Set X) : Prop :=
  A ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ ∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ
noncomputable def YuiContent {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨅ (U : ℕ → Set X) (_ : YuiCover δ A U), YuiCost s U
noncomputable def YuiMeasure {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ), YuiContent s δ A
", "parameters": [{"name": "n", "type": "ℕ"}, {"name": "E", "type": "Set (YuiEucl n)"}], "representation": "Use EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)=PiLp 2 (constant ℝ), indexed by Fin n, with its native L2 metric and Borel structure; n is a natural ambient dimension including 0. YuiSnoc appends a real coordinate and YuiHead/YuiLast recover it; YuiCylinder E is defined by these coordinates directly in EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n+1)). T003 checks the coordinate inverse and Euclidean distance identities used by all cylinder arguments, so there is no max-product metric or unproved metric replacement. The interval remains Set.Icc (0:ℝ) 1. Metric.ediam, YuiCost, YuiContent and YuiMeasure take values in ℝ≥0∞; ^ with a real exponent is ENNReal.rpow. The supremum over a nonempty witness equals ediam^s and over an empty witness equals zero, giving the prescribed empty-cover convention even at exponent zero. All uses of Hausdorff content or normalization are guarded by s>0 and δ>0. Cover sequences enumerate countable covers with empty padding; the positive-diameter construction uses a subset of ℕ to avoid duplicating finite nonempty families. dimH is native, defined as the supremum of nonnegative exponents with infinite native unnormalized Hausdorff measure; its nonnegative extended codomain gives dimH empty=0. Positive real exponents are embedded by ENNReal.ofReal only with the relevant positivity; D remains dimH E in ℝ≥0∞ and its toReal value is used only downstream of T005's finiteness. Nat casts of n and constants are finite ENNReal values. Lebesgue measure/integrals in the slicing and interval workers are volume on ℝ and the nonnegative lintegral. All five M facts are supplied by direct pinned Mathlib use, not additional premises. Background notes remain optional node-local references. N outputs are unchanged; auxiliary T001 exposes the uniform metric-space normalization calculation already used in S001 so both Euclidean and real-interval instances can share it.", "inputs": [{"id": "H001", "binder": "h_H001", "type": "0 ≤ n"}, {"id": "H002", "binder": "h_H002", "type": "E.Nonempty"}, {"id": "H003", "binder": "h_H003", "type": "IsCompact E"}, {"id": "T002", "binder": "h_T002", "type": "(∀ (k : ℕ) (A : Set (YuiEucl k)) (a : ℝ), 0 < a → YuiMeasure a A = MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure a A ∧ (dimH A < ENNReal.ofReal a → YuiMeasure a A = 0) ∧ (ENNReal.ofReal a < dimH A → YuiMeasure a A = ⊤) ∧ (YuiMeasure a A = 0 → dimH A ≤ ENNReal.ofReal a) ∧ (YuiMeasure a A = ⊤ → ENNReal.ofReal a ≤ dimH A)) ∧ (∀ (k : ℕ) (A : Set (YuiEucl k)), 0 ≤ dimH A) ∧ (∀ (k : ℕ) (A B : Set (YuiEucl k)), A ⊆ B → dimH A ≤ dimH B) ∧ (∀ (k l : ℕ) (A : Set (YuiEucl k)) (g : A → YuiEucl l), Isometry g → dimH (Set.range g) = dimH A)"}], "target": "0 ≤ dimH E ∧ dimH E ≤ (n : ℝ≥0∞) ∧ dimH E < ⊤", "explanation": "Compactness supplies a positive enclosing box size. For n≥1 retain the grid argument: C depends only on the box and n; for each fixed exponent s>n its cost C*n^(s/2)*h^(s-n) tends to zero as positive h tends to zero, with h also below the chosen mesh bound. Use N001 to get D≤n. For n=0 use the sole empty tuple and nonemptiness, and zero singleton costs. The dimension and n casts here lie in ℝ≥0∞; prove strict finiteness rather than using toReal before it is available.", "source_steps": [{"id": "S006", "text": "H003 says E is compact. Compact subsets of Euclidean space are bounded: the open balls centered at the origin with positive integer radii cover the space, so a finite subcover of E puts it inside one such ball. Hence there exists a real L>0 with E⊆[-L,L]^n. Record this existence before choosing L."}, {"id": "S007", "text": "Choose L as in F001 and set C=(2L+2)^n. By H001, n≥0; first take the branch L1: n≥1. For 0<h≤1, divide each coordinate interval [-L,L] into at most ceil(2L/h) closed intervals of length at most h. The resulting grid contains at most (2L/h+1)^n≤C h^(-n) cubes, each of diameter at most sqrt(n) h, and covers E. For any s>n the total s-cost is at most C n^(s/2) h^(s-n), which tends to zero as h decreases to zero. At each fixed target scale take h≤delta/sqrt(n) and then h arbitrarily small; H^s_delta(E)=0 at every scale, hence H^s(E)=0. N001 yields D≤s for every s>n, so D≤n. N001 also gives 0≤D. This proves the branch L1 implication; discharge L1."}, {"id": "S008", "text": "For the other branch L2: n=0, H002 and the single empty tuple give E=Eucl(0), a singleton. A singleton cover has diameter 0 and zero s-cost for every s>0, so H^s(E)=0 for all s>0. N001 gives D≤s for every s>0, and D≥0, hence D=0. Discharge L2. Since the nonnegative integer n is either zero or at least one, the two branches and F002 give 0≤D≤n, in particular finite D."}], "boundary": "Only listed inputs are project premises. The pinned Mathlib environment is freely available; no sibling proof is supplied.", "background_supplement_sha256": "1bf0b9c7347572e230e12960e1ad72681eb160b097abdd7fb42c849256a378a3", "objects": [], "representations": [], "bridges": [], "shared_inputs": [], "background_note_index": [{"id": "R002.BG001", "at": "/inference/argument/0/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For compact K⊆Eucl(n), some L>0 satisfies K⊆[-L,L]^n. Open balls in the specified metric are open, and the positive-integer-radius balls centered at the origin cover Eucl(n)."}, {"id": "R002.BG002", "at": "/inference/argument/1/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For L>0, n≥1 and 0<h≤1, the interval [-L,L] admits a partition into m=ceil(2L/h) closed subintervals of length at most h. Their n-fold products cover [-L,L]^n, number at most (2L/h+1)^n≤(2L+2)^n h^(-n), and have diameter at most sqrt(n)h."}, {"id": "R002.BG003", "at": "/inference/argument/1/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For finite K>0 and real p>0, Kh^p tends to zero as h decreases to zero, even under any additional fixed positive upper bound on h. Consequently nonnegative H^s_δ(E) bounded above by such admissible-cover costs is zero; if this holds for every δ>0, H^s(E)=0."}, {"id": "R002.BG004", "at": "/inference/argument/2/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For x∈[0,∞] and finite real b≥0, if x≤s for every real s>b then x≤b. This applies with x=D, b=n in S002 and with b=0 in S003."}]}}
